Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-06-2001||05:14 PM||||I picked up a decklid with a rear wing several days ago and thanks to Oreif I was told I need the white torsion springs.  I remeber seeing Rodney Dickmans decklid strut kit and was wondering if anyone bought and installed the kit?  I am thinking about purchasing the 2 strut kit.  I just want to know if the people who bought the kit are happy with it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||07-06-2001||09:44 PM||||I don't have em or know of anyone but if Rodney is selling them I am sure they work well.  <P>I too am getting tired of being wacked in the head now and then from weak torsion bar<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008626.htmls." TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008626.htmls.</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||3fifty||07-08-2001||01:14 AM||||I bought the dual strut kit from Rodney. They<BR>look and work great. Takes about 45min if you work slow and careful. Cut a piece of pvc pipe the length from your deck lid in the up position and the top frame of the trunk. Put a bathroom scale on the trunk ledge and put the pvc on top of the scale so you can get a acurate weight of you deck lid.<BR>Rodey will need this weight to send the proper srtuts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||07-08-2001||04:30 PM||||I have Rodney's SINGLE strut kit on both of my cars.  I also have cut away the stock tortion springs entirely.<BR>Also, I have the wing.<P>This means I have his strongest strut :P)<P>I love it, highly recomend it, and it takes like 10min to install. including cutting the old tortion bars out (with air cutter :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||rcn491||07-08-2001||06:09 PM||||I used the kit on my Ferrari 328 kit with the shock tower braces. Works great!||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||07-08-2001||06:24 PM||||I ran into two minor problems on my 86 SE with a wing. <P>First, when the lid is closed, the strut forces the lid forward and it would hit the left grill. <P>Second, the lid won't pop up when the remote truck button is hit. The latch just grabs it again.<P>Now on a friend's 85GT (same car essentially), the lid does pop just enough to clear the release and while the strut forces the lid forward, it doesn't hit the grill. I think that the body mount should be a tad lower.<P>Still, if you have no springs this is the way to go but the springs are better. ||||reg||1
